   "gap": "Supply every imported HOL rule/completeness obligation and distinguish full semantics and its nonaxiomatizability from Henkin completeness: (1) for the selected typed higher-order language (Church's system) the full (standard-model) semantics and its nonaxiomatizability are not distinguished from the proved general-model completeness; the route only says that completeness 'says nothing about which wffs are true in all standard models' (second-and-higher-order-logic-w02-p02-040.tex lines 1208-1210), and nonaxiomatizability is stated and proved only for relational full second-order validity Val_2. (2) The full-versus-Henkin comparison asserts, for the matched Henkin relational semantics, compactness ('by first-order compactness'), downward and upward Loewenheim-Skolem transfer ('transfers through the many-sorted presentation', 'with the usual language/cardinality qualifications') and non-categoricity with nonstandard selected-domain models, and for full semantics that eligible choice is valid 'only relative to adequate metatheoretic choice' (second-and-higher-order-logic-supplement.tex lines 85-89, 281, 285-291); none of these has a written proof on the route, although the imported proof boundary (inherited-12537-12673.tex lines 127-135) makes asserting compactness or a downward Loewenheim-Skolem result for the chapter's calculus conditional on carrying the first-order construction back to that rule surface.",
